	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Arathi Highlands are a high, dry country of grass, wind and grey stone that lies between the {link:hillsbrad-foothills}Hillsbrad Foothills{/link} and {link:the-hinterlands}The Hinterlands{/link}. It was here that humankind first became a nation. The fortress of {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link} rose on these plains when the tribes of men were still at war with the trolls, and every human kingdom of the world descends from it. Now the highlands belong to no one. Stromgarde, the kingdom that kept Strom's name, has fallen into ruin. The orcs hold {link:hammerfall}Hammerfall{/link} on the eastern hills, on the very ground where the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} once kept them in chains. The last soldiers of Stromgarde wait at {link:refuge-pointe}Refuge Pointe{/link} for the day they can go home.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Some twenty-eight centuries before the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link}, the human tribes of the north were scattered and at war with one another, and the Amani {link:trolls}trolls{/link} preyed upon them all. {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link}, warlord of the Arathi tribe, bound the tribes together and raised the fortress of {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link} in these highlands. The open, arid land denied the trolls the forest ambushes they favoured. In Strom the elves of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} taught a hundred humans the ways of {link:arcane-magic}magic{/link}, and together the two peoples broke the Amani in the {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link}. In later centuries the empire of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} spread across the continent and left its first city behind. The great families moved north, and the last of Thoradin's line sailed south to found the realm that became {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. The Trollbanes, heirs of a general of the Troll Wars, stayed. They named the old city Stromgarde.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:thoras-trollbane}King Thoras{/link} Trollbane is dead, and his city lies in ruins. {link:boulderfist-ogres}Boulderfist ogres{/link} and the brigands of the {link:syndicate}Syndicate{/link} hold most of {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link}, and the remnant of its army clings to a single quarter under {link:prince-galen-trollbane}Prince Galen Trollbane{/link}. At {link:refuge-pointe}Refuge Pointe{/link}, {link:captain-nials}Captain Nials{/link} gathers what strength is left, and the {link:league-of-arathor}League of Arathor{/link} prepares to take back the land by force. In the east, {link:hammerfall}Hammerfall{/link} has become an outpost of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. Its orcs fight off {link:witherbark-trolls}Witherbark trolls{/link} and Boulderfist ogres who have joined against them. {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} hunters sent by {link:vol-jin}Vol'jin{/link} seek an ancient sword in the Trollbane tomb, and the {link:defilers}Forsaken Defilers{/link} contest the rich valley of {link:arathi-basin}Arathi Basin{/link}. Beneath the earth, a voice calls out through crystal shards, begging for freedom.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The soldiers of {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link}.{/b} The last of the kingdom's army, split between the ruins of their capital and the camp at {link:refuge-pointe}Refuge Pointe{/link}.
• {b}The {link:horde}Horde{/link} of {link:hammerfall}Hammerfall{/link}.{/b} {link:orcs}Orcs{/link}, {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear trolls{/link} and {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}, at war with every other power in the highlands.
• {b}The {link:syndicate}Syndicate{/link}.{/b} Thieves and warlocks in the service of the fallen lords of {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link}.
• {b}The {link:boulderfist-ogres}Boulderfist ogres{/link}.{/b} The largest host in the highlands, from {link:boulder-gor}Boulder'gor{/link} to {link:boulderfist-hall}Boulderfist Hall{/link}.
• {b}The {link:witherbark-trolls}Witherbark trolls{/link}.{/b} Forest trolls of the south-east, the oldest enemies of Strom.
• {b}The {link:drywhisker-kobolds}Drywhisker kobolds{/link}.{/b} Diggers of the eastern gorge, and allies of the giants.
• {b}The Blackwater Raiders.{/b} Pirates of {link:booty-bay}Booty Bay{/link} stranded in {link:faldir-s-cove}Faldir's Cove{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}{link:arathor}Arathor{/link}.{/b} {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link} united the tribes and raised {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link}. From here humankind went out to found its kingdoms.
• {b}The Seven Kingdoms.{/b} As Strom declined, its nobles and its royal line left. The Trollbanes remained and ruled Stromgarde.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} {link:thoras-trollbane}Thoras Trollbane{/link} brought Stromgarde into the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}.
• {b}The Camps.{/b} After the war, the Alliance held defeated orcs in a camp in the eastern hills. {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} and {link:orgrim-doomhammer}Orgrim Doomhammer{/link} broke it open, and Doomhammer fell there.
• {b}The Fall.{/b} After the fall of Lordaeron, Stromgarde fell to ogres and brigands, and its people scattered.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Highlands",
			text = [=[• Four circles of standing stones stand across the highlands. Spirits of earth, fire, water and air walk among them.
• The soldiers of {link:refuge-pointe}Refuge Pointe{/link} have sworn not to leave the highlands until the king's banner flies over {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link} again.
• The orcs of {link:hammerfall}Hammerfall{/link} say that the black stain in the earth of their camp is the blood of {link:orgrim-doomhammer}Orgrim Doomhammer{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

