			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Thoras Trollbane was the king of {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link}, heir of the ancient house that has ruled the city since the royal line of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} left it. He was a warrior king in a land of hard soldiers. He is dead now, and his kingdom has died with him. He lies in a sealed tomb in the Sanctum behind the chapel of Stromgarde, with the sword of his house beside him.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Thoras was one of the rulers who raised the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} against the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. His house descends from Ignaeus, the general of the {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link} whose blade {link:trol-kalar}Trol'kalar{/link} earned the family its name. To the trolls of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}, the name of Trollbane is still a curse.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• He led {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link} into the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link} in the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.
• After the war, when the Alliance quarrelled over the internment camps and their cost, he took Stromgarde out of it.
• He was laid to rest with {link:trol-kalar}Trol'kalar{/link}, the sword of Ignaeus.]=],
		},
		{
